WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.805 --> 00:00:09.884 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Welcome to the Oceania capitals, episode three of four. First, I clear the
chosen names for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:10.536 --> 00:00:20.126 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Three capitals of the larger Melanesian states: the Solomon Islands, Papua New
Guinea and Vanuatu.

3
00:00:20.799 --> 00:00:23.609 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Honiara into view.

4
00:00:27.552 --> 00:00:32.498 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Honiara stands on the north coast of Guadalcanal, in the Solomon Islands.

5
00:00:33.148 --> 00:00:43.725 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
It grew out of an American base after the Second World War, and Henderson
Field, the airstrip fought over in 1942, is now its airport.

6
00:00:44.382 --> 00:00:52.010 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Honiara as a wartime airstrip that became a capital, on the island
where the Guadalcanal campaign was fought.

7
00:00:52.697 --> 00:00:56.064 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Port Moresby into view.

8
00:00:58.814 --> 00:01:07.046 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Port Moresby stands on the shore of the Coral Sea, on the south coast of New
Guinea, in the country of Papua New Guinea.

9
00:01:07.709 --> 00:01:19.307 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Named in 1873 by Captain John Moresby for his father, Admiral Fairfax Moresby,
it is one of the largest cities in the Pacific islands outside Australia and
New Zealand.

10
00:01:19.971 --> 00:01:28.028 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Port Moresby as the Coral Sea city named by an admiral's son, and the
gateway to the highlands behind it.

11
00:01:28.699 --> 00:01:32.275 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Port Vila into view.

12
00:01:34.656 --> 00:01:42.249 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Port Vila lies on a harbour on the island of Efate, in the centre of the New
Hebrides, now Vanuatu.

13
00:01:42.906 --> 00:01:53.738 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Until 1980 it was the capital of a colony ruled jointly by Britain and France,
and Cyclone Pam badly damaged it in 2015.

14
00:01:54.395 --> 00:02:01.257 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Port Vila as the shared Anglo-French capital, and the town Cyclone
Pam broke in 2015.

15
00:02:06.254 --> 00:02:15.809 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Honiara stands on Guadalcanal in the north, Port Moresby on the Coral Sea in
the west, and Port Vila on Efate in the south-east.

16
00:02:16.466 --> 00:02:26.996 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the wartime airstrip that became a capital, the Coral Sea city named
by an admiral's son, and the Anglo-French capital that Cyclone Pam broke.
